  "name": "Haul Fleet \u2014 Dispatch Policy with a Capacity-Constrained Repair Shop",
  "description": "Stage-3d: adds the SHOP as the binding constraint. The Stage-3c dispatch/overhaul layer generates the failure timing (bursty under wear-levelling, which synchronises ages; steady under naive/cohort, which stagger them). A fluid repair queue with capped throughput (shop_throughput = bays / repair_time trucks per step, ~70% utilised) then prices that timing: backlog[t] = max(0, backlog_prev + failures_this_step - shop_throughput), computed per realization, so each realization's burstiness drives its own downtime. trucks_down = min(backlog, N); cum_downtime integrates it. Insight: when the shop is the constraint, wear-levelling's clustered failures overwhelm it (queue backs up -> more downtime -> lost production) while staggered policies keep the shop fed -- the case where balanced dispatch LOSES. Run three times per dispatch_policy. The overhaul reset here is a fluid/aggregate approximation of finite repair capacity (the array primitives don't express top-k bay assignment); the relative policy comparison is driven by the failure-timing burstiness, which the per-truck layer captures. See STAGE3D_SHOP_CAPACITY.md.",
